==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|chastize}} (archaic in British English and rare in American English)

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|h₂eǵ}}
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|chastier}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|castigo}}. See also the doublets {{doublet|en|notext=1|chasten}}, {{m|en|castigate}} and cf. also {{l|en|chaste}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tʃæˈstaɪz/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪz|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|chastises|chastising|chastised}}

# To [[punish]] or [[scold]] someone.

